<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>A denial letter is the insurer’s position based on its inspection. It is not always the last word on your claim.</li>
<li>Read the exact reason for denial and the policy language cited. That tells you what evidence is missing.</li>
<li>Many Coastal Bend hail claims are TWIA claims, which follow Texas Insurance Code Chapter 2210 deadlines that differ from private insurers.</li>
